      "content": "the goblin thing is a bit of a weird way to put it lol, but i guess i get the idea of something being in there. \n\nit's just that the sound is so heavy and deliberate... it's not just a watery thump, it sounds like something solid is actually moving or shifting around inside. is it possible there's a piece of hardware or a component that actually broke off and is physically sliding around in the bottom?",
